// ---- English OIP (C1-C2) ----
DIDO.QUESTIONS['en_c1c2'] = [
  {q:"Not until the final report had been submitted and all the data meticulously cross-verified _______ the committee willing to concede that the initial hypothesis was, in fact, untenable.",o:["was","had been","were","would be"],a:0,e:"Inversion: 'was' agrees with singular 'the committee'",p:"Grammar & Syntax"},
  {q:"Suffice it to say that the board, _______ the recommendations of the auditors, decided to postpone the merger indefinitely.",o:["having considered","considered","to consider","consider"],a:0,e:"Perfect participle phrase",p:"Grammar & Syntax"},
  {q:"It was not until the advent of quantum computing, with its unprecedented capacity for parallel processing, _______ the limitations of classical encryption became terrifyingly apparent.",o:["that","which","when","where"],a:0,e:"Cleft sentence: 'It was not until ... that'",p:"Grammar & Syntax"},
  {q:"Which of the following sentences contains an example of verb phrase ellipsis?",o:["She can play the piano, and he can too.","The man who came late missed the announcement.","Having finished the race, the runners collapsed.","It was the manager who approved the proposal."],a:0,e:"'he can too' = 'he can [play the piano] too'",p:"Grammar & Syntax"},
  {q:"Scarcely _______ the lecture begun when a sudden power outage plunged the entire auditorium into darkness, forcing the professor to dismiss the class early.",o:["had","has","did","was"],a:0,e:"'Scarcely had' + past perfect inversion",p:"Grammar & Syntax"},
  {q:"The negotiations having reached an impasse, the diplomats decided to reconvene the following week. What is the function of \"The negotiations having reached an impasse\"?",o:["Adverbial clause of reason","Absolute construction","Noun clause","Relative clause"],a:1,e:"Absolute construction (subject + participle)",p:"Grammar & Syntax"},
  {q:"Far be it from me to impugn the integrity of our esteemed colleague, but _______ that his recent conduct has raised some troubling questions.",o:["suffice it to say","it suffices to say","sufficient to say","suffice to say"],a:0,e:"Fixed phrase 'suffice it to say'",p:"Grammar & Syntax"},
  {q:"Little _______ that his seemingly innocuous remark would precipitate a diplomatic crisis of unprecedented proportions.",o:["he knew","did he know","he did know","knew he"],a:1,e:"Inversion after 'Little'",p:"Grammar & Syntax"},
  {q:"A: \"I've been grappling with the ethical implications of the new AI surveillance system. On the one hand, it could enhance public safety; on the other, it feels like a step towards a dystopian panopticon.\" B: \"_______ I think we need to weigh the potential benefits against the erosion of civil liberties, but perhaps there's a middle ground.\"",o:["That's a false dichotomy.","I couldn't agree less.","You're preaching to the choir.","I see where you're coming from, but..."],a:3,e:"Acknowledge then propose a middle ground",p:"Conversation & Situational Language"},
  {q:"A: \"Would you mind terribly if I borrowed your car for the weekend?\" B: \"_______ I'm a bit hesitant, but as long as you're careful.\"",o:["Not at all.","I'd rather you didn't.","I suppose so.","By all means."],a:2,e:"Reluctant agreement: 'I suppose so'",p:"Conversation & Situational Language"},
  {q:"A: \"The professor's lecture on post-structuralism was utterly impenetrable. I felt like I was drowning in jargon.\" B: \"_______ I think his ideas are profound, but he does have a tendency to obfuscate rather than elucidate.\"",o:["You hit the nail on the head.","I beg to differ.","That's a bit of an exaggeration.","I know what you mean, but..."],a:3,e:"Partial agreement",p:"Conversation & Situational Language"},
  {q:"A: \"I'm afraid I have to recuse myself from this decision due to a conflict of interest.\" B: \"_______ That's very ethical of you. We'll find someone else.\"",o:["That's very prudent.","I'm sorry to hear that.","You're too kind.","That's outrageous."],a:0,e:"Commending ethical caution: 'prudent'",p:"Conversation & Situational Language"},
  {q:"A: \"The government's new policy on climate change is, to put it mildly, a band-aid solution. It barely scratches the surface of the problem.\" B: \"_______ I think it's a step in the right direction, even if it's not sufficient. We can't let the perfect be the enemy of the good.\"",o:["I couldn't have said it better.","I take your point, but...","You're absolutely right.","I'm not convinced."],a:1,e:"Partial agreement",p:"Conversation & Situational Language"},
  {q:"A: \"Do you think we should confront him about his plagiarism?\" B: \"_______ We need to be careful. Accusations like that can ruin a career.\"",o:["I'm in two minds about it.","That's a no-brainer.","I'm all for it.","It's not my call."],a:0,e:"'I'm in two minds' = undecided",p:"Conversation & Situational Language"},
  {q:"The CEO's _______ demeanor, while ostensibly polite, was perceived by many employees as a thinly veiled attempt to assert dominance and quell dissent.",o:["obsequious","recalcitrant","perspicacious","intransigent"],a:0,e:"obsequious = overly submissive / flattering",p:"Vocabulary & Precision"},
  {q:"The politician's promise to lower taxes was widely dismissed as a _______ victory, as it would ultimately lead to cuts in essential public services.",o:["Pyrrhic","Sisyphean","Herculean","Promethean"],a:0,e:"Pyrrhic victory = a win at too great a cost",p:"Vocabulary & Precision"},
  {q:"The scientist's findings were initially met with skepticism, but they eventually gained _______ acceptance once independent replication confirmed the results.",o:["ubiquitous","ephemeral","unequivocal","pernicious"],a:2,e:"unequivocal = unambiguous / definite",p:"Vocabulary & Precision"},
  {q:"The two theories are _______ linked; one cannot be fully understood without the other.",o:["inextricably","inexplicably","inexorably","infallibly"],a:0,e:"inextricably = inseparably",p:"Vocabulary & Precision"},
  {q:"The author's use of _______ language, full of obscure references and archaic terms, made the novel inaccessible to all but the most erudite readers.",o:["sesquipedalian","sycophantic","obsequious","perspicacious"],a:0,e:"sesquipedalian = using long / obscure words",p:"Vocabulary & Precision"},
  {q:"The committee's decision was _______ with controversy, as it seemed to favor corporate interests over environmental concerns.",o:["fraught","rife","teeming","laden"],a:0,e:"fraught with = full of",p:"Vocabulary & Precision"},
  {q:"Identify the error: \"The committee, after much deliberation and having considered all the evidence, decided that the proposal was not only impractical but also it would be financially ruinous.\"",o:["having considered","was not only impractical","but also it would be","financially ruinous"],a:2,e:"Parallelism: 'not only ... but also' — 'it would be' breaks parallel structure",p:"Error Identification"},
  {q:"Identify the error: \"The reason for his abrupt resignation was because he felt his contributions were being systematically overlooked.\"",o:["reason for","was because","being systematically overlooked","his contributions"],a:1,e:"Redundancy: 'The reason ... was because' → 'was that'",p:"Error Identification"},
  {q:"Identify the error: \"The new policy, which aims to reduce carbon emissions and promoting renewable energy, has been met with both praise and criticism, with some arguing that it is too little too late.\"",o:["which aims","promoting","has been met","too little too late"],a:1,e:"Parallelism: 'promoting' → 'promote' (to match 'reduce')",p:"Error Identification"},
  {q:"Identify the error: \"The data collected from the experiment suggests that the new drug is effective, but further trials are needed to confirm its safety.\"",o:["data","suggests","are needed","its"],a:1,e:"'data' is plural → 'suggest'",p:"Error Identification"},
  {q:"The proliferation of social media has been hailed as a democratizing force, yet its impact on public discourse is _______(25).",o:["unequivocal","ambivalent","negligible","pernicious"],a:1,e:"ambivalent = mixed / conflicting",p:"Cloze Test"},
  {q:"_______(26), the algorithms that curate our feeds are designed to maximize engagement, often at the expense of accuracy.",o:["Nevertheless","Furthermore","Consequently","Similarly"],a:1,e:"Furthermore = adds another point",p:"Cloze Test"},
  {q:"_______(27) the potential for connection, the fragmentation of shared reality is a pressing concern.",o:["Notwithstanding","Given","Despite","Because of"],a:2,e:"Despite + noun phrase",p:"Cloze Test"},
  {q:"_______(28), we must consider whether the benefits outweigh the societal costs.",o:["Ultimately","Conversely","In contrast","Similarly"],a:0,e:"Ultimately = concluding",p:"Cloze Test"},
  {q:"What is the author's primary argument in the passage on AI and creativity?",o:["AI will eventually replace human creativity.","Creativity is solely about generating novel combinations.","Human judgment is essential to creativity and cannot be replicated by AI.","Machines are better at generating variations than humans."],a:2,e:"Human judgment is essential to creativity",p:"Reading Comprehension"},
  {q:"The word \"empirically dubious\" in the passage suggests that the author believes the opposing view is:",o:["not supported by evidence","morally wrong","theoretically sound","widely accepted"],a:0,e:"not supported by evidence",p:"Reading Comprehension"},
  {q:"Which of the following best describes the author's tone?",o:["Sarcastic and dismissive","Objective and neutral","Passionate and assertive","Ambivalent and uncertain"],a:2,e:"Passionate and assertive",p:"Reading Comprehension"},
  {q:"The author mentions \"philosophically impoverished\" to:",o:["criticize the opposing view as lacking depth","praise the opposing view for its simplicity","suggest that philosophy is irrelevant","argue that AI is philosophically advanced"],a:0,e:"Criticize the opposing view as shallow",p:"Reading Comprehension"},
  {q:"What is the main idea of the passage on globalization?",o:["Globalization has benefited all nations equally.","Globalization has both positive and negative distributional effects.","Globalization is entirely harmful.","The environmental costs of globalization are negligible."],a:1,e:"Both positive and negative distributional effects",p:"Reading Comprehension"},
  {q:"The word \"exacerbated\" in the passage is closest in meaning to:",o:["alleviated","worsened","stabilized","ignored"],a:1,e:"exacerbated = worsened",p:"Reading Comprehension"},
  {q:"According to the passage, who are the primary losers of globalization?",o:["Owners of capital","Skilled workers in developed nations","Unskilled workers in both developed and developing countries","The global poor who bear environmental costs"],a:2,e:"Unskilled workers are the losers",p:"Reading Comprehension"},
  {q:"What does the author imply about the current global system?",o:["It is fundamentally just.","It needs to be reformed to address inequalities.","It should be abolished entirely.","It has no environmental impact."],a:1,e:"It needs reform",p:"Reading Comprehension"},
  {q:"What is the speaker's attitude toward the proposal?",o:["Enthusiastic support","Cautious skepticism","Outright hostility","Indifference"],a:1,e:"Cautious skepticism",p:"Listening Comprehension",l:"Transcript 1: speaker reacting to a proposal"},
  {q:"How did the speaker feel after the lecture?",o:["Confused and frustrated","Humbled and inspired","Bored and indifferent","Angry and defensive"],a:1,e:"Humbled and inspired",p:"Listening Comprehension",l:"Transcript 2: speaker after a lecture"},
  {q:"What is the main point of disagreement between the two speakers?",o:["Whether the episode was worth watching","Whether the ending was contrived or satisfying","Whether the writers are talented","Whether the series should continue"],a:1,e:"Contrived vs. satisfying ending",p:"Listening Comprehension",l:"Transcript 3: conversation about a final episode"},
  {q:"What does the speaker advise?",o:["To immediately implement policy changes","To ignore the report entirely","To be cautious about using the report for policy","To expand the sample size immediately"],a:2,e:"Be cautious about policy decisions",p:"Listening Comprehension",l:"Transcript 4: speaker on a report's conclusions"}
];

// ---- Math English Program ----
DIDO.QUESTIONS['math_en'] = [
  {q:"If July 23, 2022 is Saturday, then August 23, 2022 is",o:["Sunday","Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Friday"],a:2,e:"July has 31 days; +31 days = +3 weekdays (Sat → Tue)"},
  {q:"Ant and Bat are the same height. Kat's height is 161 cm. The average (mean) of the heights of Ant, Bat and Kat is 171 cm. What is Ant's height?",o:["161 cm","166 cm","176 cm","183 cm","191 cm"],a:2,e:"(2x + 161)/3 = 171 → x = 176 cm"},
  {q:"Factor 625 - x^4.",o:["(25 + x^2)^2","(25 + x^2)(5 - x)(5 + x)","(25 + x^2)(5 + x)^2","(25 - x^2)^2","(5 - x)^2(5 + x)^2"],a:1,e:"Difference of squares twice: (25−x²)(25+x²) = (5−x)(5+x)(25+x²)"},
  {q:"The ratio of apples to bananas in a box is 3 : 2. The total number of apples and bananas in the box cannot be equal to",o:["40","55","175","160","72"],a:4,e:"Total must be a multiple of 5; 72 is not"},
  {q:"In the set of real numbers, which of the following is the range of the function f(x) = { -2x, if x > 0; x + 3, if x <= 0 }?",o:["{y | y >= -3}","{y | y <= 3}","{y | 0 < y <= 3}","{y | y < 0 or y >= 3}","all real numbers"],a:1,e:"x>0 gives −2x < 0; x≤0 gives x+3 ≤ 3 → range y ≤ 3"},
  {q:"The restaurant sells 5-inch and 8-inch (in diameter) pizzas. At least how many 5-inch pizzas are needed to replace an 8-inch pizza?",o:["2","3","4","5","6"],a:1,e:"Area ∝ d²; 8²/5² = 64/25 ≈ 2.56 → at least 3"},
  {q:"What is the y-intercept of a line that passes through the points (1, 3) and (-2, -4)?",o:["-1","-0.66","0","0.5","0.66"],a:4,e:"Slope = 7/3; b = 3 − 7/3 = 2/3 ≈ 0.66"},
  {q:"Ann and Betty go on a 30 km run. They both usually run at 10 km/h. If Ann runs at 0.5 times her usual speed, and Betty runs at 1.5 times her usual speed, how many more hours does it take Ann than Betty?",o:["1","2","3","4","6"],a:3,e:"Ann: 30/5 = 6 h; Betty: 30/15 = 2 h; difference = 4 h"},
  {q:"The expression 6 + 2 * 0 - 9 equals",o:["-54","-12","-9","-3","12"],a:3,e:"6 + 0 − 9 = −3"},
  {q:"Which of the following expressions is not equivalent to 3x + 6?",o:["3(x + 2)","(-9x - 18) / -3","(1/3)(3x) + (2/3)(9)","(1/3)(9x + 18)","3x - 2(-3)"],a:2,e:"C = x + 6 ≠ 3x + 6"},
  {q:"If (xy^3) * (y^-1 x^3) = 81, then the possible value for x^2 y is",o:["1","3","9","27","81"],a:2,e:"x⁴y² = 81 → (x²y)² = 81 → x²y = 9"},
  {q:"Find the value of 1 - 2 + 3 - 4 + 5 - 6 + ... + 2019 - 2020 + 2021 - 2022.",o:["-1010","-1011","1010","1011","1110"],a:1,e:"1011 pairs of (a − b) = −1 each → −1011"},
  {q:"How many roots larger than 1 does x^2 - 3x + 2 have?",o:["None","One","Two","Three","Cannot be determined"],a:1,e:"Roots are 1 and 2; only 2 > 1"},
  {q:"If 3(1/9)^(1-x) = (1/27)^(x-3), then x =",o:["0","13/5","2","-2","-13/5"],a:2,e:"3·(3⁻²)^(1−x) = (3⁻³)^(x−3) → x = 2"},
  {q:"Given the functions f(x) = x + 6 and g(x) = x^2 - 2, what is the value of (f ∘ g)(3)?",o:["7","9","10","13","79"],a:3,e:"g(3) = 7; f(7) = 13"},
  {q:"A plane ticket is $436.00. Over three weeks the price rises 5%, falls 10%, then rises 20%. What is the cost in 3 weeks (to the nearest cent)?",o:["$412.02","$457.80","$494.42","$501.40","$523.20"],a:2,e:"436 × 1.05 × 0.90 × 1.20 = $494.42"},
  {q:"This year only 29 students entered the drawing for a talent show host. What is the probability either Hanna or Jake is selected?",o:["1/841","2/841","1/58","1/29","2/29"],a:4,e:"2 favorable outcomes out of 29 → 2/29"},
  {q:"Let i denote the complex number sqrt(-1). Which of the following is equal to (1 - 3i) / (2 - i)?",o:["1 + 3i","(-1 - 5i) / 5","5 - 5i","1 + i","None of the above"],a:4,e:"(1−3i)/(2−i) = (5−5i)/5 = 1−i (not listed)"},
  {q:"The ordered pairs {(3, 2), (1, 2), (3, -1), (5, 1), (4, 5)} represent a relation that is not a function. What change would make it a function?",o:["Replace (1, 2) with (2, 3).","Replace (3, 2) with (3, 5).","Replace (4, 5) with (4, 3).","Replace (3, -1) with (2, 1).","Replace (5, 1) with (5, 3)."],a:3,e:"Removes the duplicate x = 3 mapping"},
  {q:"Which of the following is an equation of the line perpendicular to the line passing through (-2, 5) and (3, -5)?",o:["y = 2x - 5","y = -1/2 x - 3","y = -2x + 5","y = 1/2 x + 7","None of the above"],a:3,e:"Given slope = −2; perpendicular slope = 1/2"},
  {q:"If 3x + 17 = 5, then 2x + 4 =",o:["-4","-2","0","2","4"],a:0,e:"x = −4; 2x + 4 = −4"},
  {q:"Which of the following is a value of x for which x^2 + x - 6 = 0?",o:["-4","-3","-2","-1","1"],a:1,e:"(x+3)(x−2) = 0 → x = −3 or 2"},
  {q:"Allen can mow the lawn in 5 hours, and Betty can mow the lawn in 4 hours. How many hours will it take them to mow the lawn together?",o:["1","2 2/9","4","4 1/2","5"],a:1,e:"1/(1/5 + 1/4) = 20/9 = 2 2/9 h"},
  {q:"If a mixture is 3/7 alcohol by volume and 4/7 water by volume, what is the ratio of alcohol to water?",o:["3/7","4/7","3/4","4/3","7/4"],a:2,e:"(3/7) : (4/7) = 3 : 4"},
  {q:"If 40% of students have blue eyes and 20% of those with blue eyes have brown hair, what percent of the total have brown hair and blue eyes?",o:["4%","8%","16%","20%","32%"],a:1,e:"0.40 × 0.20 = 0.08 = 8%"},
  {q:"The perimeter of an isosceles triangle ABC is 42. The equal sides AB and AC are each three times as long as the third side. What are the lengths of each side?",o:["21, 21, 21","6, 6, 18","18, 21, 3","18, 18, 6","4, 19, 19"],a:3,e:"3x + 3x + x = 42 → x = 6; sides 18, 18, 6"},
  {q:"For x > 0, y > 0, which is equivalent to (3x^(3/2) y^3 / (x^2 y^(-1/2)))^(-2)?",o:["9x / y^7","9y^7 / x","x^2 / 9y^3","x / 9y^7","x^(1/2) / 3y^(7/2)"],a:3,e:"Inside = 3x^(−1/2)y^(7/2); raised to −2 → x/(9y⁷)"},
  {q:"Let f be a linear function such that f(3) = -1 and x-intercept is 2. Find f(-4).",o:["6","4","7","5","8"],a:0,e:"Line through (3,−1) and (2,0): y = −x + 2 → f(−4) = 6"},
  {q:"You own 2 hats, 3 shirts, 2 pants and 5 shoes. How many different ways can you dress yourself with hat, shirt, pant and shoe?",o:["12","20","30","60","80"],a:3,e:"2 × 3 × 2 × 5 = 60"},
  {q:"GPA for the first three years are 3.2, 3.1 and 3.4. What is the minimum GPA during the last year to attain a 3.0 average (same credits each year)?",o:["2.3","2.5","2.8","3.0","3.2"],a:0,e:"(3.2+3.1+3.4+x)/4 = 3.0 → x = 2.3"}
];

// ---- Science EP ----
DIDO.QUESTIONS['sci_en'] = [
  {q:"A 5 kg block is pushed up a rough 30° incline at 10 m/s (coefficient of kinetic friction 0.2). Calculate the distance it travels up the plane before coming to rest.",o:["5.1 m","8.5 m","12.3 m","4.2 m","10.0 m"],a:1,e:"½mv² = mg(sinθ + μcosθ)·d; d = v²/[2g(sinθ+μcosθ)]"},
  {q:"A car accelerates uniformly from rest to 72 km/h in 10 s, travels at that speed for 20 s, then decelerates to rest in 5 s. What is the total distance?",o:["300 m","400 m","500 m","600 m","700 m"],a:2,e:"72 km/h = 20 m/s; sum the three phase distances"},
  {q:"Two blocks of 4 kg (on a frictionless table) and 6 kg (hanging) are connected over a frictionless pulley. What are the acceleration and the tension?",o:["5.88 m/s², 23.52 N","4.90 m/s², 29.40 N","5.88 m/s², 35.28 N","3.92 m/s², 23.52 N","4.90 m/s², 35.28 N"],a:0,e:"a = m₂g/(m₁+m₂) = 5.88 m/s²; T = m₁a = 23.52 N"},
  {q:"A uniform 150 g meter stick is pivoted at its center. A 200 g mass hangs at the 10 cm mark. At which mark must a 300 g mass hang to balance it?",o:["60 cm","70 cm","80 cm","90 cm","50 cm"],a:3,e:"Torque balance about the 50 cm pivot"},
  {q:"A 2 kg object at 5 m/s collides head-on (elastic) with a 3 kg object at 2 m/s in the opposite direction. What are their velocities after the collision?",o:["-1 m/s, 6 m/s","-2 m/s, 5 m/s","1 m/s, -4 m/s","-1 m/s, 4 m/s","-2 m/s, 3 m/s"],a:4,e:"Elastic collision: conserve momentum and kinetic energy"},
  {q:"A 500 Hz source moves toward a stationary observer at 20 m/s (speed of sound 340 m/s). What is the apparent frequency?",o:["469 Hz","531 Hz","500 Hz","550 Hz","480 Hz"],a:1,e:"f' = f·v/(v−v_s) = 500×340/320 ≈ 531 Hz"},
  {q:"An object is placed 20 cm in front of a concave mirror of focal length 15 cm. What is the magnification?",o:["0.5","2.0","3.0","1.5","4.0"],a:2,e:"1/f = 1/u + 1/v → v = 60 cm; |m| = v/u = 3"},
  {q:"Resistors of 6 Ω, 3 Ω and 2 Ω are in parallel, in series with a 4 Ω resistor and a 12 V battery. What is the total current?",o:["1.0 A","1.5 A","2.0 A","2.5 A","3.0 A"],a:0,e:"R_parallel = 1 Ω; total 5 Ω; I = V/R"},
  {q:"A 2000 W, 220 V heater runs 4 hours a day for 30 days. What is the cost if electricity is 2.5 baht per kWh?",o:["300 baht","450 baht","600 baht","750 baht","900 baht"],a:2,e:"2 kW × 4 h × 30 = 240 kWh × 2.5 = 600 baht"},
  {q:"A block floats in water with 60% of its volume submerged. What is its density, and what fraction is submerged in a liquid of density 800 kg/m³?",o:["600 kg/m³, 75%","400 kg/m³, 50%","600 kg/m³, 60%","800 kg/m³, 80%","500 kg/m³, 62.5%"],a:0,e:"Density = 0.6×1000 = 600 kg/m³; 600/800 = 75%"},
  {q:"A hydraulic lift has small piston area 10 cm² and large piston area 500 cm². If 100 N is applied to the small piston, what mass can the large piston lift?",o:["50 kg","100 kg","500 kg","1000 kg","5000 kg"],a:4,e:"Pascal: F₂ = F₁·(A₂/A₁)"},
  {q:"A 200 g metal at 150°C is dropped into 500 g water at 25°C; final temperature is 30°C. What is the specific heat of the metal? (water = 4200 J/kg°C)",o:["300 J/kg°C","420 J/kg°C","450 J/kg°C","500 J/kg°C","350 J/kg°C"],a:4,e:"Heat lost by metal = heat gained by water"},
  {q:"A plant cell is placed in a solution with a higher solute concentration than its cytoplasm. Which best describes the resulting change?",o:["The cell swells and becomes turgid.","The cell shrinks and undergoes plasmolysis.","The cell bursts because the wall cannot withstand pressure.","The cell remains unchanged.","The cell swells and bursts."],a:1,e:"Water leaves the cell → plasmolysis"},
  {q:"Which correctly describes the process of translation in protein synthesis?",o:["DNA is transcribed into mRNA in the nucleus.","mRNA is decoded by ribosomes to synthesize a polypeptide chain.","tRNA carries amino acids to the nucleus to form proteins.","DNA replicates itself to form two identical molecules.","mRNA is spliced to remove introns before leaving the nucleus."],a:1,e:"Translation: ribosome decodes mRNA → polypeptide"},
  {q:"A patient has a severe vitamin K deficiency. Which physiological process is most directly affected?",o:["Oxygen transport in the blood","Blood clotting cascade","Immune response to pathogens","Regulation of blood glucose levels","Filtration of blood in the kidneys"],a:1,e:"Vitamin K is needed for the clotting cascade"},
  {q:"In a dihybrid cross AaBb x AaBb, what is the probability of an offspring homozygous dominant for both traits?",o:["1/16","3/16","9/16","1/4","1/8"],a:0,e:"AABB = (1/4)(1/4) = 1/16"},
  {q:"A man with blood type AB marries a woman with blood type O. What are the possible blood types of their offspring?",o:["A and B only","AB and O only","A, B, and AB only","A, B, AB, and O","A and O only"],a:0,e:"AB × O → offspring A or B only"},
  {q:"A color-blind man (XcY) marries a carrier woman (XCXc). What is the probability their daughters will be color-blind?",o:["0%","25%","50%","75%","100%"],a:2,e:"Daughters get Xc from father; 50% get Xc from mother"},
  {q:"Which best describes the mechanism of a GMO such as Bt corn?",o:["Selectively bred over generations to resist pests.","Injected with pesticides to kill insects.","Contains a bacterial gene producing a protein toxic to specific pests.","Exposed to radiation to induce pest resistance.","Modified to grow faster and need less water."],a:2,e:"Bt corn: bacterial gene → insect-toxic protein"},
  {q:"In snapdragons, flower color shows incomplete dominance (RR red × WW white). If F1 is self-pollinated, what is the F2 phenotypic ratio?",o:["1 Red : 2 Pink : 1 White","3 Red : 1 White","1 Red : 1 White","2 Red : 1 Pink : 1 White","1 Red : 1 Pink : 2 White"],a:0,e:"Incomplete dominance F2 ratio = 1 : 2 : 1"},
  {q:"A couple has a child with cystic fibrosis (autosomal recessive). Neither parent has the disorder. What are the parents' genotypes?",o:["Both homozygous dominant.","One homozygous dominant, one heterozygous.","Both heterozygous carriers.","One homozygous recessive, one heterozygous.","Both homozygous recessive."],a:2,e:"Both must be heterozygous carriers"},
  {q:"Nondisjunction in meiosis II produces an egg with an extra X chromosome, fertilized by a normal sperm (Y). What abnormality results?",o:["Turner syndrome (XO)","Klinefelter syndrome (XXY)","Down syndrome (Trisomy 21)","Triple X syndrome (XXX)","Jacob's syndrome (XYY)"],a:1,e:"XXY = Klinefelter syndrome"},
  {q:"Which statement best explains why energy transfer between trophic levels is only about 10%?",o:["Most energy is lost as heat during metabolic processes.","Most energy is stored in biomass.","Most energy is transferred to decomposers.","Most energy is used for reproduction.","Most energy is lost during photosynthesis."],a:0,e:"Most energy is lost as heat in metabolism"},
  {q:"In the food chain Grass → Grasshopper → Frog → Snake → Hawk, if grass contains 50,000 kJ, how much energy is available to the hawk?",o:["5,000 kJ","500 kJ","50 kJ","5 kJ","0.5 kJ"],a:3,e:"50,000 × (0.1)⁴ = 5 kJ"},
  {q:"A cell has a cell wall, chloroplasts, and a large central vacuole. Which conclusion is most accurate?",o:["It is a prokaryotic cell.","It is an animal cell.","It is a fungal cell.","It is a plant cell.","It is a bacterial cell."],a:3,e:"Cell wall + chloroplasts + vacuole = plant cell"},
  {q:"Which process requires ATP to move molecules against their concentration gradient?",o:["Simple diffusion","Osmosis","Facilitated diffusion","Active transport","Passive transport"],a:3,e:"Active transport requires ATP"},
  {q:"A plant is exposed to high light intensity but low CO₂ concentration. What limits photosynthesis and how is oxygen production affected?",o:["Light is limiting; O₂ production increases.","CO₂ is limiting; O₂ production plateaus.","Temperature is limiting; O₂ production decreases.","Water is limiting; O₂ production stops.","Chlorophyll is limiting; O₂ production increases."],a:1,e:"Low CO₂ limits photosynthesis → O₂ plateaus"},
  {q:"Which describes a mutualistic relationship?",o:["A tick feeding on a dog.","A clownfish living among sea anemone tentacles.","A tapeworm in a human intestine.","A lion hunting a zebra.","A barnacle attaching to a whale."],a:1,e:"Clownfish and anemone both benefit (mutualism)"},
  {q:"In the human nephron, which structure is primarily responsible for ADH-regulated reabsorption of water and salts?",o:["Glomerulus","Bowman's capsule","Proximal convoluted tubule","Loop of Henle","Collecting duct"],a:4,e:"Collecting duct: ADH-regulated water reabsorption"},
  {q:"Which best describes the role of the cerebellum in the human nervous system?",o:["Controls voluntary movements and higher cognition.","Regulates involuntary actions like heart rate and breathing.","Coordinates muscle movements, balance, and posture.","Acts as a relay station for sensory information.","Controls hormone release from the pituitary gland."],a:2,e:"Cerebellum: coordination, balance, posture"}
];


